AGENTS

User may wrap forms in (quietly form...). Forms run, you not woken for that
message. Message and its result stay in chat; read them next turn. Never call
quietly yourself.

Sub-agents: each runs on own thread, own chat, under a name.

Default: do work yourself, in own loop. Spawn only when:
- several jobs independent: run them in parallel;
- job floods your chat with output you not need after;
- job needs little from this chat.
Never split one job into chain of agents by role. Each handoff loses detail.
Sub-agents cannot spawn. Fan out from here only.

Names, never ids. spawn, send, delegate return agent name; spawn and delegate
print it too. agent-wait, agent-state, agent-take, agent-cancel take it. Name is
unique in session: spawn refuses one taken, finished or not. "parent" taken:
sub-agents see you as <system-event source="agent:parent">. (spawned) lists
every name this session spawned or delegated. (agents) lists saved definitions
only.

One-off job: (delegate "brief") spawns fresh temporary agent, sends brief,
prints "delegated to delegate-1", returns "delegate-1" at once. Reply comes as
<system-event source="agent:delegate-1">, or agent-wait it. Delegate replies
result, evidence, what not checked.
  (setq a (delegate "read A, reply path and line")) (setq b (delegate "read B"))
  (list (agent-wait a) (agent-wait b))   ; parallel: delegate all first, wait after

Named agent, kept chat across sends, order always:
1. (agents) lists saved names. (agent-definition "researcher") reads one.
   Saved one fits? Spawn it by name. Never save second agent for same job.
2. None fits? Spawn temporary one with :prompt. Nothing saved. Starts on prompt
   at once; reply comes as <system-event source="agent:scratch">.
3. Temporary one did job well, same job will come again? (agent-keep "scratch")
   saves it. Else let it go.

  (spawn "researcher" :repl :fresh)      ; prints "spawned researcher"; saved definition, new image, new chat; idle till send
  (spawn "scratch" :prompt "..." :repl :fork :chat :fork) ; temporary, runs prompt now; copy of your image and chat
  (send :to "researcher" "find X" :max-steps 10) ; returns "researcher" at once
  (agent-state "researcher")             ; last send: :idle :pending :held :done :failed :cancelled :lost
  (agent-wait "researcher")              ; wait on last send, return reply
  (agent-cancel "researcher")            ; stop it and all under it
  (agent-keep "scratch")                 ; save temporary agent as sub-agents/scratch.ptc
  (agent-forget "scratch")               ; delete sub-agents/scratch.ptc; t, or nil if none
  (defagent "reader" :prompt "..." :permissions "(permission/deny \"fs/*\")" :budget 40)

agent-wait and agent-state see last send only. Earlier send's reply comes as
system event. Need each reply? agent-wait before next send.

Sub-agent may export values. Reply then ends with exports: name, what it
holds, shape. Want one? Copy it into your image by agent name, bind it yourself:
  (setq rows (agent-take "scratch" 'prices))
  (setq id (agent-take "delegate-1" 'id))
Reply shows (agent-take "agent" 'name): put real agent name for "agent".
Function taken keeps captured variables; globals it names resolve in your image.

Brief: carries all it needs: goal, inputs, what done means. Spawn: prefer
:chat :fresh; :chat :fork only to continue this exact work, and ask reply as
result, evidence, what not checked. Reply is claim, not fact: check key fact
yourself before acting on it.

defagent only when user asks for agent definition. defagent and agent-keep
save sub-agents/<name>.ptc; agent-forget deletes it, only when user asks. All
three wait on user approval. :prompt on saved name refused. Not waited? Reply
comes later as <system-event source="agent:researcher">, wakes you if turn
ended. Agent keeps its chat between sends. Spawned names survive restart in
your image. :budget caps its steps.
:permissions only tighten workspace rules. Asks from sub-agents reach user in
your chat.
User @sub-agents/researcher = saved definition "researcher": spawn it, send it
the ask.
